    definition: "An adjective is a word that describes a noun or pronoun. The book groups adjectives into seven kinds: proper, quality/state, number/quantity, distributive, demonstrative, interrogative and possessive. A proper adjective is made from a proper noun (a name of a country, language, place, person) and is always written with a capital letter.",
